course: dictionary
lesson: 10320
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives tractor two meanings, and the sentence around the word tells you which one is meant. «Gulls follow a tractor ploughing a field» is about the farm vehicle, because ploughing a field is what a farm machine does.
explain: Look for clues. Words like «ploughing», «field», «trailer» and «drive» point to a meaning. The second meaning is a large truck cab that pulls a trailer, sometimes called a «tractor-trailer». If the sentence is about a long road journey with a load behind the cab, the truck meaning is more likely.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «a farm vehicle ploughing a field» make sense? Yes. Does «a truck cab ploughing a field» make sense? No, so the farm meaning is right here.
fact: A tractor is a strong farm vehicle with big back wheels.
fact: Farmers use a tractor to pull ploughs, trailers and other machines.
fact: A tractor can also be a large truck cab that pulls a trailer.
fact: «Tractor» is a noun: one tractor, two tractors.
fact: Useful phrases: «drive a tractor», «a tractor and trailer», «tractor ride».
exercise: «Gulls follow a tractor ploughing a field, because ploughing turns up worms and grubs.» What is a tractor in this sentence? | A bird that eats worms | A large truck cab that pulls a trailer | A tall tree at the edge of the field | *A strong farm vehicle with big back wheels
exercise: Find and copy one word in «Gulls follow a tractor ploughing a field» that tells you what the tractor is doing. | Gulls | *ploughing | worms | field
exercise: Sam says a tractor is always a farm vehicle. Is he right? | *No, a tractor can also be a large truck cab that pulls a trailer | No, a tractor is a kind of bird | Yes, but only in towns | Yes, always
test: «The lorry driver stopped his tractor-trailer at the motorway services.» What does tractor mean here? | A bird that eats worms | *A large truck cab that pulls a trailer | A tall tree | A strong farm vehicle with big back wheels
test: «Never ride on a tractor without permission.» What does this sentence teach you? | *Children should stay safe and not ride on farm machines without permission | Riding on tractors is the best fun on a farm | Tractors are only for towns | Permission is a kind of farm machine
exam: «Some farm tractors steer themselves using GPS.» Which meaning fits best? | A farm dog that herds sheep | *A strong farm vehicle with big back wheels | A kind of satellite | A large truck cab that pulls a trailer
